{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1511967-new-orleans","id":1511967,"title":"New Orleans","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-05-17T21:14:38-07:00","id":1511967,"title":"New Orleans","content":"I know New Orleans is covered for VtR and maybe for Beast, but it seems such a shame that more wasnt done with the Big Easy, especially for Sin Eater. <br /> <br /> So I was wondering what people here have done with New Orleans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-17T22:21:26-07:00","id":1511973,"title":"","content":"The VtR material is mostly pre-Katrina, and with how later 1E and 2E VtR developed there are a number of things I would do differently for a New Orleans setting now. Changeling 2E has some material for the French Market in the core. I'm planning to have a stop here in an upcoming I-10 cross country road trip campaign for a group of mortals and have had a few concepts bouncing around for that but haven't run it yet. A random creepy observation I had the other day that could make for a fun setting detail was a house painted as a clown's face in the Bywater, with windows as eyes and a painted on smile and nose beneath them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27841,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27841-haintbleu","user":"HaintBleu","date":". 05-18-2023, 08:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27841-haintbleu","name":"HaintBleu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-17T22:22:20-07:00","id":1511974,"title":"","content":"I know Changeling has Tumbletown Market. Which I adore. But that also has egresses anywhere there's a street market, so I've only really used it for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-18T01:02:56-07:00","id":1511981,"title":"","content":"Pandora's Book for Promethean 1e has an adventure that takes place in New Orleans. There's also some notes, and an adventure in the Beast core book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I created a google map with all of the official Chronicle of Darkness locations that you can find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/maps/d/u/0/edit?mid=1ADtXovdxb5zVAMieQDfRXUw5m_9EigPj&amp;ll=35.65578786133324%2C-109.13453443883256&amp;z=5\" target=\"_blank\">here!</a>\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27756-arkhaam","name":"Arkhaam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27756_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-18T18:18:35-07:00","id":1512069,"title":"","content":"Sadly we never used New Orleans in any vtr games, but we did use it as a source to build up our nearest city.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-18T18:32:17-07:00","id":1512073,"title":"","content":"I can't believe that I forgot this. The first time I ran CtL 1e, it was set in 1920s New Orleans. The players ended up running a speak easy, with a connected Hollow. The Wizened was experimenting with making moonshine from goblin fruit. <br /> <br /> A lot of that game was dealing with the lost generation, and the effect of WWI on dreams, the Hedge, and Arcadia","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I created a google map with all of the official Chronicle of Darkness locations that you can find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/maps/d/u/0/edit?mid=1ADtXovdxb5zVAMieQDfRXUw5m_9EigPj&amp;ll=35.65578786133324%2C-109.13453443883256&amp;z=5\" target=\"_blank\">here!</a>\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27756-arkhaam","name":"Arkhaam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27756_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-25T11:50:23-07:00","id":1512757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaintBleu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1511967-new-orleans?p=1511973#post1511973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The VtR material is mostly pre-Katrina, and with how later 1E and 2E VtR developed there are a number of things I would do differently for a New Orleans setting now. Changeling 2E has some material for the French Market in the core. I'm planning to have a stop here in an upcoming I-10 cross country road trip campaign for a group of mortals and have had a few concepts bouncing around for that but haven't run it yet. A random creepy observation I had the other day that could make for a fun setting detail was a house painted as a clown's face in the Bywater, with windows as eyes and a painted on smile and nose beneath them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/2364/City-of-the-Damned-New-Orleans?affiliate_id=321987\" target=\"_blank\">City of the Damned: New Orleans</a> is one of the books that would gain most if it were to receive a Vampire: the Requiem 2nd edition coverage. It would be quite interesting to hear what you would different from the first edition's description of the city? <br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27293-cabaal","name":"Cabaal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27293_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-27T22:32:47-07:00","id":1513041,"title":"","content":"Mostly the fact that City of the Damned was an early 1E book means than a lot of bloodlines that would fit the setting were printed after the city book.(the Apollinaire being the most obvious example, but I would also make the Geheim an element of the city, introduced by Jacques St. Germain).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27841-haintbleu","name":"HaintBleu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}